            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>During the walkthrough, we found leakage on the following items:

-All doors

-Receptacles

-Electrical panel

-Header joist

-All windows

The air leakage results of the house are high, this situation increases the energy consumption to heat the house. We notice that a lot of air comes from the front door. We recommend the replacement of the unit. The same situation is present on the other exterior doors of the house.

</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>At the moment of the assessment the insulation of the main walls was R-22. We recommend adding insulation to reach the city of Whitehorse standard of R-28. </mainWalls>
                <ceilingsCathedral>At the moment of the evaluation, the attic insulation was R-40. We recommend adding some insulation to reach the city of Whitehorse standard of R-60. Attic insulation protects your home against heat loss caused by the stack effect in winter and against the excessive heat transfer from the attic in the living space in the summertime. </ceilingsCathedral>
                <windows>At the moment of the inspection, we noticed that all windows leaks and some are broken. We also notice condensation and frosting on the windows. We recommend the replacement of all windows by triple panes  ENERGY STAR CERTIFIED product and suitable for the northern climate and Canada Zone 3.</windows>
                <doors>We noticed air leakage coming from all the doors. The main entrance door was very leaky. We recommend the replacement of the units by ENERGY STAR CERTIFIED product.</doors>
            </RURComments>
